/-!
# The volume of an ellipsoid in shape-matrix form

For positive-definite `Q`, the Lebesgue measure of `{x | (x − q)ᵀ Q⁻¹ (x − q) ≤ 1}` is
`V_n √det Q`, `V_n = π^(n/2) / Γ(n/2 + 1)` the volume of the unit `n`-ball: [1, Sec. I (volume)]'s
`vol(B)/√det Q⁻¹` and [2, Eq. 2]'s `τ_n √det E`. The set is the ellipsoid generated by
`Q^(1/2)` (`mem_ofShape_iff`), a square generator, whose volume is `Ellipsoid.volume`
(`volume_eq`) at the shape `Q` (`ofShape_eq`).

## Inputs
* `Q` – shape matrix
* `q` – center

## Hypotheses
* `hQ` – `Q` positive definite

## Conclusion
* the volume of the set is `V_n √(det Q)`

## References

* [1] A. Halder. "On the parameterized computation of minimum volume outer ellipsoid of Minkowski
      sum of ellipsoids". 2018 IEEE Conference on Decision and Control (CDC), 2018.
* [2] M. Černý. "Goffin's algorithm for zonotopes". Kybernetika, 2012.
-/

